<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Deliberately empty.  A free Apple ID cannot carry extra entitlements, and
	the signature that actually authorises the app is added by whoever
	sideloads the IPA.  This file exists only so codesign embeds an
	entitlements blob plus its DER form, exactly as the milestone-0 smoke test
	(the one bundle that is known to install) was signed.

	Keep it SHORT.  XML forbids two consecutive hyphens inside a comment, and
	the operating system's entitlements parser rejects the whole file when it
	sees one - see PORT_FINDINGS 7.17.  The previous revision carried a 29-line
	comment and still worked, but it made the embedded blob 1474 bytes against
	the smoke test's 372, so there is nothing to gain from length here.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
